  "limitations": "Both unchanged stock suite entry points pass in C and Rust on i686 SSE2. T/testC and suite native libraries remain absent. The x87 model is an exploratory baseline, not the declared Rust arithmetic profile. Five huge traceback cases time out in both bounded processes and remain incomplete. Native Linux x64 all.lua still fails at big.lua:11, and Windows entry points retain main.lua:53. Full Lua 5.1 parity, complete C/auxiliary APIs, production native loading, broader numeric/debug/GC/resource behavior, later dialects and integrations remain open."
